{
  "id": 21,
  "type": "table",
  "title": "Sound camp overview + limits (v7)",
  "description": "Per-camp overview with the currently-active dB limit and a status flag. Click a camp's id or campname to open the camp view. id/campname/tier come from the 'sensors' Google Sheet (Infinity); max_dbc is the sheet's max_dbc_now helper column (current sound_schedule limit for the camp's zone+tier, computed with NOW() in the spreadsheet). status = LCmax_r3m minus max_dbc: OK (<=0), ! (0-5 dB over), !!! (>5 dB over). LCmax trend is a sparkline of LCmax (sensor_sound_LCImax) over the panel range; ts_updated is the absolute time of the last sensor sample. LCmax_r3m is the median of LCImax over 3m. It adds two per-sensor offsets from the sheet: global_calibration_offset_dbc (permanent calibration of the sensor hardware) and the location offset dbc_diff_abs (dbc_reference - dbc_sensor). Each offset is ignored (treated as 0) when its source cells are blank, non-numeric or outside +/-30 dB, so a half-filled calibration row can no longer inflate a camp. The generic correction_factor (+5%) has been removed - sensors are calibrated individually instead. The LCmax trend sparkline is NOT offset (per-device offsets cannot be applied to the trend frames; a constant shift is invisible on an autoscaled sparkline anyway).",
  "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "h": 30,
    "w": 24
  },
